Package: anbernic-rg353x-headphone-detect
Version: 1.0.0
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, alsa-utils, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54~)
Conflicts: anbernic-rg353x-alsa-ucm, rg353-headphone-detect
Replaces: anbernic-rg353x-alsa-ucm, rg353-headphone-detect
Maintainer: Andrew Rossignol <andrew.rossignol@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/aarossig/anbernic-rg353x-headphone-detect
Description: Automatic headphone jack detection daemon for Anbernic RG353 series
 Event-driven Bash daemon that monitors headphone insertion/removal on
 RK3566/RK817 handheld devices (RG353V, RG353VS, RG353M, RG353P) and switches
 ALSA Playback Mux between Speaker and Headphones. Applies the correct output
 at boot. Ideal for retro gaming, direct ALSA, and headless environments.
